## 1. Existing Codebase Analysis Summary

### 1.1 Architecture Overview

The current AiBus backend is a well-structured **modular monolith** built with:

| Layer | Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Runtime | Node.js + TypeScript | Type-safe backend |
| Framework | Express 5 | HTTP layer |
| ORM | Prisma (PostgreSQL) | Database access |
| Cache/Locks | Redis (ioredis) | Caching, distributed locks |
| Queue | BullMQ | Background jobs |
| Validation | Zod | Schema validation |
| Auth | JWT (access + refresh tokens) | Token-based auth |
| Logging | Pino | Structured logging |
| Security | Helmet, HPP, CORS, Rate Limiting | Production hardening |
| Docs | Swagger/OpenAPI | API documentation |

### 1.2 Module Pattern (Existing Convention)

Every module follows this strict pattern:
```
src/modules/<module>/
  ├── <module>.routes.ts       # Express Router with middleware chain
  ├── <module>.controller.ts   # Thin controller (delegates to service)
  ├── <module>.service.ts      # Business logic (Singleton pattern)
  └── <module>.validation.ts   # Zod schemas + exported types
```

**Key Patterns Observed:**
- **Singleton services** via `static getInstance()` pattern
- **Zod validation** via `validate()` middleware
- **Standardized API responses** via `ApiResponse` utility (`success`, `created`, `paginated`, `noContent`, `error`)
- **Centralized error hierarchy** via `AppError` base class with specific subclasses
- **Child loggers** per module via `logger.child({ module: 'name' })`
- **`getPrismaClient()`** for database access (lazy singleton)
- **Role-based auth** via `authenticate` + `authorize(...roles)` middleware
- **Idempotency** via `Idempotency-Key` header middleware
- **Request tracing** via `X-Request-Id` header

### 1.3 Database Schema (Current State)

**Existing Models (18):**
`User`, `RefreshToken`, `City`, `Booking`, `BookingSeat`, `BookingPassenger`, `SeatHold`, `Payment`, `Cancellation`, `Refund`, `Ticket`, `WebhookEvent`, `ProviderTransaction`, `WalletTransaction`, `Notification`, `AuditLog`, `IdempotencyRecord`

**Existing Enums:**
`UserRole` (CUSTOMER, OPERATOR_AGENT, SUPPORT_AGENT, ADMIN, SUPER_ADMIN), `UserStatus`, `BookingStatus` (16 states), `HoldStatus`, `PaymentStatus`, `CancellationStatus`, `RefundStatus`, `RefundDestination`, `TicketStatus`, `NotificationChannel`, `NotificationType`, `NotificationStatus`, `WalletTransactionType`, `IdempotencyStatus`

**Existing Roles (already in schema):**
- `CUSTOMER` — end users
- `OPERATOR_AGENT` — bus operator staff (not yet utilized)
- `SUPPORT_AGENT` — customer support (not yet utilized)
- `ADMIN` — platform admin (not yet utilized)
- `SUPER_ADMIN` — super admin (not yet utilized)

### 1.4 What Exists vs. What's Missing

| Area | Current State | Admin Gap |
|---|---|---|
| **Authentication** | ✅ JWT with refresh token rotation, bcrypt, family-based revocation | ❌ No admin-specific login, no MFA, no session management |
| **Authorization** | ✅ `authenticate`, `authorize`, `hasMinimumRole` middleware | ❌ No granular permissions (only role-based, no permission-based) |
| **User Management** | ✅ Basic profile (get/update self) | ❌ No admin user CRUD, no suspend/activate, no bulk ops |
| **Booking Management** | ✅ Create, get, user bookings | ❌ No admin listing, no filters, no status override, no bulk actions |
| **Payment Management** | ✅ Create intent, verify, webhook | ❌ No admin payment listing, no manual reconciliation, no settlement |
| **Cancellation/Refund** | ✅ Check cancellability, cancel seats | ❌ No admin-initiated cancellation, no manual refund processing |
| **City Management** | ✅ List + sync from GDS | ❌ No admin CRUD, no activate/deactivate control |
| **Dashboard/Analytics** | ❌ None | ❌ Revenue, booking, user, payment, system analytics |
| **Operator Management** | ❌ None | ❌ Full operator CRUD, document management |
| **Route/Schedule Mgmt** | ❌ None (GDS-driven) | ❌ Admin view/override/configuration of routes |
| **Offers/Coupons** | ❌ None | ❌ Full promotion engine |
| **Support/Complaints** | ❌ None | ❌ Ticket system, escalation, resolution tracking |
| **Notifications Admin** | ❌ BullMQ workers exist but no management | ❌ Template management, broadcast, history, retry |
| **Content/Config** | ❌ None | ❌ Dynamic config, feature flags, CMS |
| **Reports/Exports** | ❌ None | ❌ Downloadable reports, scheduled reports |
| **Audit Logs** | ✅ AuditLog model exists | ❌ No admin API to view/search/filter audit logs |
| **System Health** | ✅ Basic health check | ❌ No admin system monitoring dashboard |

