## 8. Cross-Cutting Production Concerns

### 8.1 Performance & Caching Strategy

| Endpoint | Cache Strategy | TTL |
|---|---|---|
| Dashboard overview | Redis cache | 60s |
| Revenue analytics | Redis cache | 300s |
| City list (admin) | Redis cache | 3600s |
| Operator list | Redis cache | 600s |
| Audit log queries | No cache (real-time) | — |
| Booking/Payment lists | No cache (real-time) | — |

### 8.2 Security Measures

- **All admin routes behind `authenticate` + `authorize`** (role check)
- **Granular permissions** via `authorizePermission()` for sensitive operations
- **Admin-specific rate limiting** (200 req/min for reads, 50 req/min for writes)
- **IP logging** on every admin action
- **Automatic audit trail** on all mutations via middleware
- **SUPER_ADMIN-only access** for system config, feature flags, user deletion
- **Sensitive field masking** in audit logs (passwords, tokens, secrets)

### 8.3 Database Optimization

- All new models indexed on common query patterns (status, dates, foreign keys)
- Paginated queries with `skip`/`take` + total count
- Aggregate queries for dashboard use `$queryRaw` for performance
- No N+1 queries — proper `include` usage

### 8.4 Error Handling

- All admin services throw typed `AppError` subclasses
- Admin-specific errors: `AdminActionDeniedError`, `InvalidConfigError`, `ReportGenerationError`
- All errors include `requestId` for tracing

### 8.5 Logging

- Every admin service creates a child logger: `logger.child({ module: 'admin-<submodule>' })`
- All admin mutations log the acting admin ID, target resource, and action
- Sensitive data (passwords, tokens) never logged

